record.content:
The Direction Cosines define the orientation of a vector with respect to a coordinate reference frame.  Each direction cosine is the cosine of the angle between the vector and its corresponding  coordinate axis.  Let us first look at a  two dimensional example.

\begin{figure}
\epsfig{file=figure1.eps}
\caption{2D - Direction Cosines}
\label{01}
\end{figure}
